  "readme": "## README.md\n# Air Quality Archive\n\nCloud-native copies of air quality observations, preserved independently of\nthird-party dashboards. This is a [Portolan](https://github.com/portolan-sdi/portolan-spec)\nv0.2.0 catalog on STAC 1.1.0. Machines start at `catalog.json`.\n\nPublished at https://data.source.coop/walkthru-earth/opensensor-space/catalog.json and s3://us-west-2.opendata.source.coop/walkthru-earth/opensensor-space/ (anonymous, us-west-2).\n\n| Collection | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| [OpenAQ Station Measurements](openaq/README.md) | OpenAQ archive measurements as GeoParquet, partitioned by location, year and month |\n| [OpenAQ Station Aggregates and H3 Cells](openaq-aggregates/README.md) | Hourly, daily and yearly station means with WHO, US EPA and EU levels, plus H3 resolution 1 to 9 map cells |\n\n## License\n\nEach collection and item declares its own license. OpenAQ data licenses differ per\nsource provider, see [OpenAQ licenses](https://docs.openaq.org/resources/licenses).\n\n## Provenance\n\nThis catalog is a mirror. Data comes from the public\n[OpenAQ archive](https://registry.opendata.aws/openaq/). It is maintained by Walkthru Earth (https://github.com/walkthru-earth).\n",
  "_review": [
    "summaries.item_count: parts overlap, so this is max(part), not the sum \u2014 enviroplus-health/ 250, enviroplus/ 127600, openaq-aggregates/ 1262604, openaq/ 159434. Sum them only once the parts are known to be disjoint."
  ],
